---In some cases it may be useful for plugins to retrieve additional data on-demand from an external source, rather than
---bundling the data with the plugin, or to send data to an external location.
---
---Plugins can make use of the HTTPRequest type to perform `GET` and `POST` requests, allowing them to retrieve and send
---data if needed.
---
---Requirements: To ensure safety and prevent misuse, plugins must request the `httpAccess` permission in their manifest
---in order to be able to create or trigger HTTPRequests, like so:
---
---Additionally, the URLs that will be used must also be specified in the manifest, however you just need to specify the
---base URLs instead of all endpoints:
---
---Warning: Specifying malformed URLs or URL shortener/redirect addresses will cause your plugin to be rejected.
---@class HTTPRequest
---@field data string (Read-only) Contains the response received from the remote server, or an empty string if the request is pending or has failed.
---@field header string (Read-only) Contains the header received from the remote server, or an empty string if the request is pending or has failed.
---@field cancelled boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this request has been cancelled by the user.
---@field finished boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this request has been completed, regardless of whether it succeeded or not.
---@field successful boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this request has been completed successfully.
---@field failed boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this request has failed due to an error.
---@field timedOut boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this request has failed due to not getting a response from the specified target.
---@field responseCode integer (Read-only) HTTP response code received from the target.
---@field errorCode integer (Read-only) HTTP error code received from the target.
---@field errorInfo string (Read-only) If `failed` is true, this contains additional information regarding the cause of the error.
---@field progress number? (Read-only) Returns a value in a 0..1 range representing the download progress for this request. If the server does not provide expected download size information, this is instead nil.
---@field url string (Read-only) The address this request is attempting to communicate with.
---@field downloadedBytes integer (Read-only) Number of bytes downloaded from the target so far.
---@field downloadTotalBytes integer (Read-only) Number of bytes expected to be downloaded from the target. Note in some cases this may be 0 despite an in-progress download, as some servers do not provide the necessary information.
HTTPRequest = {}

---Creates a request pointing at a combination of the baseURL and an optional path.
---@param baseURL PluginURL Base URL address to concatenate `path` to. Specified in the manifest and accessed via the `Plugin.urls` table.
---@param path? string Optional additional path to concatenate to the baseURL.
---@return HTTPRequest
function HTTPRequest.new(baseURL, path) end

---Triggers a `GET`/`POST` request to the remote endpoint specified by this request, and optionally sets up callbacks to
---track its completion and/or progress.
---
---Warning: Calling this method on an active request will trigger an error.
---@param completionCallback? fun(self: HTTPRequest) Callback triggered when this request finishes, regardless of success. Receives this request as its parameter.
---@param progressCallback? fun(self: HTTPRequest) Callback triggered whenever this request's download progress changes. Receives this request as its parameter.
function HTTPRequest:Get(completionCallback, progressCallback) end

---Triggers a `GET`/`POST` request to the remote endpoint specified by this request, and optionally sets up callbacks to
---track its completion and/or progress.
---
---Warning: Calling this method on an active request will trigger an error.
---@param data string
---@param completionCallback? fun(self: HTTPRequest) Callback triggered when this request finishes, regardless of success. Receives this request as its parameter.
---@param progressCallback? fun(self: HTTPRequest) Callback triggered whenever this request's download progress changes. Receives this request as its parameter.
function HTTPRequest:Post(data, completionCallback, progressCallback) end

function HTTPRequest:Cancel() end

---Warning: Calling this method on an active request will trigger an error.
---@param key string
---@param value string
function HTTPRequest:AddHeader(key, value) end
